  "description": "What the index computes from admitted objects (docs/spec.md section 11.2), never at admission. rooted is sets of tokens a host holds, each as it stores it (the stored hex under chain, and in transaction-v1.json): a first token is rooted by the outpoint its input spends, and a later one when the host holds the token it spends, back to the first; the result does not depend on order. chain is the transaction vectors' vault folded from seq 0, each token consistent, with the size of the set and the number stale the fold gives. carriers are admitted carriers on secret-tree outputs, each with the status the chain's listings and its outpoint's row give, the first that applies of retracted, superseded, mismatched, listed, unlisted. outpoints are those rows, and the row of a swept outpoint no carrier spent, which has no winner: the winner is the lowest commitment in hash byte order, kept as a running minimum; others are the lowest of the rest, at most 8, and more counts what was not kept. bounded is one row fed twelve commitments out of order. dropped is a row of two carriers whose winner the host then drops, and a lower commitment admitted afterwards: nothing on the outpoint is answered again.",
